The Committee likewise agreed to seek the comments of the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) and the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD) on the bills and to invite them to the next TWG meeting scheduled on August 23, 2017 (Wednesday), at 9:30 A.M., at Room 5, Ramon V. Mitra Bldg.

The Technical Working Group (TWG), chaired by the Honorable Jose Enrique Garcia III, conducted its second meeting on House Bill No. 4498, introduced by Rep. Maximo Rodriguez, Jr., and House Bill No. 5540, introduced by Reps. Michael Romero and Enrico Pineda, which seek to amend the Magna Carta for Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs).

The TWG first reviewed the substitute bill for the two bills which was prepared by the Secretariat, based on the discussions and agreements arrived at during the 1st TWG meeting on August 8, 2017.  Rep. Garcia stated that some of the sections had to be revisited as the same have not been finalized yet. 

1)  The Department of Budget and Management (DBM) obliged to submit its official position on the funding provisions of the bills, and likewise on its formulation of the rules for the effective implementation of the entitlement of the MSMEs to at least 10% of the total procurement value of goods and services supplied to the government;
2)   The TWG approved renaming the MSME Centers to MSME Negosyo Centers;
3)  On their proposed membership in the Board of the Small Business Corporation (SB Corp.):
â€¢	The Government Service Insurance System (GSIS) had no objection;
â€¢	Atty. Joseph De Sunia of the Social Security System (SSS) said that the agencyâ€™s official comment will be submitted by September 6, 2017;
4)  Rep. Enrico Pineda agreed to one (1) re-appointment for the Board of the SB Corp., and functioning on a hold-over capacity of the incumbent directors;
5)  On the proposed deletion in the 2nd paragraph of Section 11-B of the law of the phrase â€œsubject to compliance with the rules and regulations to be issued by the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP) and the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC)â€�, Ms. Tayag of BSP pointed out the importance of putting in place the financial accountability  of SB Corp.  She informed the body that they are finalizing their comments which will be sent to the TWG within the week.
6)  On the proposed additional capitalization and funding of the SB Corp.: 
